     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""exp_25 depth_canon -- the numerical-composition control and eps_cond
     3	(plan_depth_canon.md v8 §1 Tier 2 (ii) + eps_cond, §6 test 21b).
     4	
     5	For the first ``--n-items`` items of an evaluation loader and each registered column
     6	offset d in {64, 128, 256, 384, random in [1, W-1]}, A = canon(md) and
     7	B = canon(rot_d(md)) are pushed through the SAME loaded checkpoint with the SAME fixed
     8	per-item noise, and compared stage by stage: conditioning tensors, the one-step DiT
     9	velocity, the latent after the single Euler step, the decoded waveform after
    10	clamp(-1, 1). relL2 / relLinf use ``src/tools/depth_canon_stats`` (pinned
    11	denominators, A is the reference). Tier 1 (canonical recovered-depth sha256 of A == B)
    12	is recorded for the same items. eps_cond = max fp32 conditioning relL2; PASS <= 1e-5.
    13	
    14	GPU for the registered run (the Planner launches it); CPU-testable on a toy stack.
    15	
    16	Written by the exp_25 Coder seat (Claude Opus, max effort) per plan_depth_canon.md v8 §1/§6/§8.
