worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_worklog.md:164:- **Bridge effect (the finding)** — C4L vs historical legacy-loop B-F@40k at K8: T60 +0.212, C50 +0.0317, EDT +2.71, R@1 −0.268 — the recipe/environment delta (8×8 rung + batched orbit + chunk-shared RoPE + L40 + torchrun DDP) shifts the absolute level measurably. **This is precisely why the review-mandated C4L bridge exists: orbit inferences (R1/trend) run against C4L, same recipe, and are untouched; cross-era comparisons vs historical rows would conflate this shift with the orbit effect and are excluded by the table's non-interchangeability rule.**
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_worklog.md:338:- **Finding:** under the exp_11 recipe (8×8, batched orbit, chunk-shared RoPE, L40), frame averaging HURTS acoustic parameters and yields only a marginal retrieval edge — REVERSING the legacy-recipe result (exp_07 B-F > B-V on all metrics, confirmed exp_10 decomposition). The fa advantage is recipe-contingent. Leading mechanism candidates for the closing analysis: chunk-shared vs per-angle RoPE draws (the disclosed Q6 recipe change), micro-batch-8 BN statistics × conditioning interplay, orbit-averaged conditioning under the batched execution. Caveats: one training seed per arm; own-protocol evals per convention.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_worklog.md:349:**R2 decomposition (Cn/an − C4L/a4 = eval + train + interaction), T60/EDT:** the θ=0 degradation is **training-side dominated** (train T60 +0.408/+1.024/+0.737 and EDT +2.497/+4.660/+3.122 for n=8/16/32 — reproducing R1's inverted-U at C16), with a lineage-independent **eval-side penalty ~+0.45 T60 / ~+1.0 EDT that saturates already at a8** (C4L: eval +0.456/+0.451/+0.453 for a8/a16/a32; legacy exp_07 B-F replicates: +0.488/+0.480/+0.480, loop-era baseline, batched cross cells — era-mixed until cell 3684155 lands) and a consistently negative interaction. Cross contract note: fa-arm sets were incomplete (only a4 off-diagonals submitted initially) — 6 completing cells queued (3684137–40, 3684143–44); C8/C16/C32 cross numbers are PROVISIONAL until their full sets validate.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_worklog.md:351:**Synthesis with q9:** training WITH finer orbits hurts θ=0 accuracy (training-side), and *evaluating* any C4-trained model with finer averaging also hurts (eval-side, saturating) — while in-group invariance is exact. Combined with the VANL reversal (fa itself underwater vs vanilla in this recipe), the working hypothesis: orbit averaging in *training* is the damaging ingredient in the L40/8×8/batched recipe, candidates = chunk-shared RoPE draws + BN-8 micro-batch statistics under averaged conditioning.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_worklog.md:357:Full cross matrix (T60 delta vs own protocol, s42 K8 @40k): C4L at a8/a16/a32 = +0.456/+0.451/+0.453 (flat in n); C8 at a4/a16/a32 = +0.107/+0.047/+0.042; C16 at a4/a8/a32 = +0.079/+0.023/+0.000; C32 at a4/a8/a16 = +0.012/+0.026/+0.004. **Asymmetry:** finer-trained arms are near-robust to ANY eval orbit change (all ≤ +0.107, shrinking with training orbit); only the C4-trained model pays a large, immediately-saturating toll under finer eval orbits. Legacy exp_07 B-F @40k vs its own batched-era a4 baseline (cell 3684155, same pin 89f24cd): a8/a16/a32 T60 +0.490/+0.481/+0.482, R@1 −0.47/−0.71/−0.62 — replicates C4L within ~0.03 across lineage AND recipe. R2 decomposition unchanged from the provisional numbers (training-side dominated, inverted-U at C16; negative interaction). Evidence: 6 completing cross cells (3684137–40, 3684143–44) + legacy baseline committed with sidecars; manifest updated.
