worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_codex_plan_review.md:7:1. **BLOCKING — The historical C4 comparator is not a true single-delta control.** Exp_07 C4 was trained on 2×A6000 ([launch record](/n/fs/gatrdp/codespace/FLAC/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_07_fa_scratch_claude/bf_scratch_launch.sh:5)); exp_11 targets 2×L40 ([plan](/n/fs/gatrdp/codespace/FLAC/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/plan_fa_orbit.md:65)). Same seed does not remove GPU/kernel/environment-dependent numerical divergence, which is especially material when training-seed replication is out of scope. **Fix:** train a contemporaneous C4 bridge arm to 40k on the same commit, environment, GPU type, and staging conditions as C8/C16/C32, or run all new arms on the original hardware/software stack. Pin and record GPU UUID/type, CUDA/cuDNN, package hash, source SHA, initializer hash, and first-batch/RNG traces. Without this control, describe the result as a historical cross-run comparison, not an “only orbit changed” causal result.
