    94	- **Dated the code change:** the batched orbit + chunk-shared RoPE draws landed **2026-08-06** (`1479304` batched-orbit invariant_conditioning; `8094d60` disclose the chunk-shared draw). Our FA training ran **7/18–7/23 (0→40k)** and **8/1–8/5 (40k→67.5k)** — both legs finished BEFORE that commit.
    95	- **Therefore (a)** our entire B-F arm trained on the legacy **per-angle** loop, so exp_10 did NOT silently change method at the 40k resume boundary — a confound that would have been very hard to detect after the fact, now ruled out by date; **(b)** exp_11's C4L trained with **chunk-shared** draws (micro-8 → all three non-zero angles share one draw). The two arms are NOT the same method at training time; the frame-averaged conditioning differs by ~4% (magnitude corroborated by exp_11's own probe log: eval-bf16 deviation 0, train fp32 and bf16 both ≈3.7–3.9%).
    96	- **Matched, so NOT suspects:** effective batch 64 and BN statistics (SyncBN on both sides → BN 64 for both), ViT grad-checkpointing (numerics-identical). Remaining differences: draw structure (above), rung topology 32×2 vs 8×8, hardware, data order.
    97	- **Forward-looking consequence:** retraining FA on the A6000 TODAY would not reproduce our own July arm — current code at micro-32 gives `64//32 = 2` angles per chunk (partial sharing), a third regime. Reproducing July requires `FRAME_AVG_MAX_FWD_SAMPLES = 32`. **Any FA arm must record the effective chunk plan (cap, micro-batch, orbit size); the same config file a month apart is not the same method.**
