    99	## 2026-08-11T20:57:29-04:00 — A6 PRE-REGISTERED (Yixun approved: "做，两个 ckpt 都做"): rotation head-to-head, vanilla vs FA
   100	- **Claim under test:** vanilla FLAC degrades under yaw rotation while C4 FA does not — the strongest TRUE form of the equivariance narrative, measured head-to-head instead of argued architecturally.
   101	- **Grid:** checkpoints = vanilla P1@40k (matches A4's budget), vanilla anchor@87.5k (our strongest vanilla), FA B-F@40k (per-angle chunk plan, announcement 06). Rotations = 0 deg (have), 90 deg (C4 orbit member), 45 deg (off-orbit control). Seeds 42-46, K=8 first then K=1. Protocol otherwise pinned: EMA, cfg 1.0, steps 1, full unseen split, per-scene mean; each arm under its own cond-method.
   102	- **PRE-REGISTERED READOUT:** per checkpoint, the rotation delta = metric(90 deg) - metric(0 deg), 5-seed with sigma_c. PREDICTION: |delta| ~ 0 for FA on all metrics (its C4 sweeps already spread <=1e-3); |delta| >> 0 for both vanilla checkpoints. The 45 deg cell is the off-orbit control: FA is C4-exact only, so FA should ALSO move at 45 deg — if it does not, something is wrong with the rotation plumbing rather than right with the model.
   103	- **Interpretation limit fixed in advance:** this measures robustness to a rotated test distribution. It does NOT re-open the canonical-orientation comparison (A4), and a vanilla arm trained WITH yaw augmentation is not in scope (no such arm exists).
