   106	- **At 90 deg (C4 orbit member), 5-seed deltas vs unrotated — K=8:** vanilla P1@40k T60 +0.311 / C50 +0.032 / EDT +1.654 / R@1 -0.268; vanilla anchor@87.5k T60 +0.491 / C50 +0.033 / **EDT +5.829** / R@1 -0.470; **C4 FA@40k T60 -0.000 / C50 +0.000 / EDT +0.003 / R@1 -0.006 — flat to three decimals.** K=1 concordant (FA -0.002/+0.000/+0.000/+0.010).
   107	- **At 45 deg (off-orbit control) ALL THREE degrade, FA included** (FA K8 T60 +1.438 / EDT +2.108). This is the pre-registered validity check: FA is C4-exact only, so a flat 45-degree cell would have meant broken plumbing, not a better model. The plumbing is sound.
   108	- **Head-to-head under 90-degree rotation, matched budget (K=8):** FA@40k 8.202 / 0.978 / 38.796 / R@1 5.381 vs vanilla P1@40k 9.304 / 1.041 / 42.304 / 4.905 -> **FA wins all four, by wider margins than unrotated.** Against our BEST vanilla (anchor@87.5k, 2.2x the budget): FA still wins T60 (8.202 vs 8.784), C50 (0.978 vs 0.999) and EDT (38.80 vs 41.78), losing only R@1 (5.381 vs 6.489, the anchor's budget advantage).
   109	- **Notable:** the stronger the vanilla model, the MORE it loses under rotation (anchor EDT +5.83 vs P1@40k +1.65) — canonical-orientation quality does not transfer to rotated inputs.
   110	- This is the equivariance claim in its strongest TRUE form and it does not depend on resolving the exp_11 discrepancy.
