worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_22_loc_meshgrid_claude/loc_meshgrid_2026-11-02_15-39-42_codex_plan_r2_review.log:890:   221	Canonicalization baseline for OrbitRIR (deepest depth-panorama pixel rolled to the left edge before every model input; invariance = shifted eval panoramas canonicalize to the same image). Bookkeeping in `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/` (plan v15, notebook, ledger, Codex artifacts). Launch kit: `depth_canon_launch.sh` (gates: HEAD pin, 48-file pin manifest, config contract, tie audit, NAS, GPU memory floor 12 GiB per card with `shared` occupancy and co-tenants disclosed, W&B identity, pinned `WANDB_MODE=offline`, SMOKE projection cap 300 h) armed by `depth_canon_autolaunch.sh` (GO token → 3 clean polls → SMOKE → FULL); guard suite `depth_canon_guardtests.sh` (227 cases, `GUARD_NAS_READONLY=1`). Traps learned: **never edit a bash script while it is executing** (bash reads by byte offset — the launcher and the watcher run for days); committed SMOKE evidence JSONs are FULL-gate candidates (guard fixtures clear them); the `flac` env's wandb 0.15.4 cannot create ONLINE runs against the current server (`upsert_run → server_settings_introspection` → None) — every `--logger wandb` run in `flac` must set `WANDB_MODE=offline` until the env is upgraded with Yixun's approval; a shared A6000 next to a 100 %-utilization co-tenant runs the recipe 1.6–5× slower (6–19 s/step vs 3.9). Reviews by Codex (`depth_canon_codex_code_r*.md`); see `HANDOFF.md` for pids, ETDs and the campaign plan. **Campaign traps (2026-10-29):** the registered composition probe must be run AT the campaign pin on a clean tree (`depth_canon_collect.py::probe_reasons` binds `source_sha == pin`) — run it after the pin commit and keep its JSON untracked until the campaign ends; its pre-registered ε_cond bound 1e-5 FAILED at 8.12e-5 for a numerical reason (float32 rotation roundoff × `dist_embedder` frequencies up to 2^10; Tier 1 exact; quarter turns bit-exact) — the adjudication (report as registered vs a plan v16 re-calibration) is Yixun's and open; a `pgrep -f depth_canon_eval_run.sh` guard in the launching shell matches that shell itself — rely on the driver's flock. The AR seen split (`acousticroom_seeneval*.json`) carries ONE sub-threshold item (idx 1194, `Office/Office_idx_15/S009_R092_hybrid_IR.wav`, −60.77 dBmax vs the −60 dB `is_silence` cut in `src/data/dataset.py`) that `SampleDataset.__getitem__` silently replaces by a random item, so every exp_25 S-block (seen-split) cell is refused by the evaluator's positional assignment guard by design (the unseen split has none; every seen-split number produced in this repo before exp_25 silently contained one substituted item) — S-block handling is Yixun's open decision. **Table-regen trap (2026-10-31):** `model_comparison.md` has only ever been regenerated on neuronic (`/n/fs/gatrdp/codespace/FLAC`); 23 rows — the 10 `exp_14 Z` rows (raws never force-added), the 12 exp_11 rows (`exp11_validate_rows.py` re-hashes checkpoints that exist only there and refuses the absolute neuronic `ckpt_path` elsewhere) and the 62.5k K=8 screen file — resolve only there, so on the A6000 box the generator refuses rc 4 (row regression) then rc 3 (exp_11 both-K gate). Never retract them with the overrides without Yixun's explicit order; the exp_25 rows themselves resolve from git alone (`dump_check="receipt"`, `check_link=False`). After the merge, exp_25 records go to `localization-exp` in the main checkout.
