     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""exp_25 depth_canon -- the evaluation cell manifest ("cell classes as data",
     3	plan_depth_canon.md v9 §5): every generative cell of the campaign as one row, in the
     4	registered priority order T, T-dup, C4+45, R, D-i, D-ii, S, P1-pin, YAW-pin, TRAJ.
     5	
     6	Deterministic, no I/O beyond reading nothing at all: ``build_manifest()`` is a pure
     7	function of the constants below and eval_FLAC's own ``build_output_paths`` (which names
     8	each cell's metrics stem, hence its dump directory). ``--write`` (re)writes
     9	``depth_canon_cells.json``; ``--check`` exits 1 if the committed file has drifted.
    10	
    11	A row carries the evaluator argv EXCEPT ``--ckpt-path`` (a local farm link, named after
    12	the resolved checkpoint) and ``--dump-scored-waveforms <ROOT>`` (iff the cell dumps);
    13	the driver ``depth_canon_eval_run.sh`` adds those two at run time. ``dump`` is true for
    14	every row (A3 pending: the driver's ``--no-dump-blocks`` deselects a block's dumps).
