   260	## 10. Residual risks
   261	- **Retrieval thresholds.** Tier 3 thresholds for retrieval (10 % of P1's Δ_C4 ≈ 3.5–6.8 items) are within numerical jitter, so `pass_c4` on R@k may turn on 1–2 item flips. It is reported as registered.
   262	- **E2 at K8** compares against a neuronic cell.
   263	- **B-F timing.** Co-tenant times for B-F cells have not been measured on this box since August, so the ETA range stays wide until chunks 3–4.
   264	- **NAS stalls.** The NAS (CIFS) can stall; any item substitution is caught by `--expected-stream-count` and the registry.
   265	- **exp_22 dependency.** exp_22's backend amendment and its watcher's reservation support belong to an exp_22 round (decision 7), not to exp_35 code. The exp_22 watcher stays suspended until then.
    78	
    79	CANON’s composition control is not a valid numerical control for B-F. In the committed CANON probe, the evaluation-control p99 values at the quarter-turn offsets are exactly zero, while d64/random are nonzero:
    80	
    81	```text
    82	d128 = d256 = d384 = 0
    83	d64 = 0.014003...
    84	random = 0.011007...
    85	pooled = 0.010524...
    86	```
    87	
    88	The resulting CANON rows are visible at [depth_canon_results.md:21](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_results.md:21). CANON makes the quarter-turn inputs identical after canonicalization; B-F instead permutes and sums the four C4 conditioner passes, so its own arithmetic floor must be measured.
    89	
    90	The faithful analog is:
    91	
    92	```text
    93	A = FA(md)
    94	B = FA(rotate_d(md))
    95	d ∈ {128, 256, 384 panorama columns}
    96	```
    97	
    98	using the exact B-F checkpoint/config, four registered angles, cap 64, bf16 evaluation conditioning, fixed item stream and the same probe stages. No canonicalization should run.
    99	
   100	B-F’s Tier 2 conclusion should then be split:
   101	
   102	- **Tier 2-C4:** registered invariance verdict at 90°/180°/270°, judged against B-F’s own FA composition control and the absolute cap; T-dup remains exact.
   103	- **45° and random yaw:** report waveform distances descriptively as off-orbit non-invariance. They are outside the C4 invariance claim. They may exceed the C4 threshold “by construction,” but that is not a failed C4-invariance verdict.
   104	- **Tier 3:** still applies the registered C4 and random-yaw rules, so the overall B-F Tier 3 verdict is expected to fail if `|Δ_R| > sd(m_Z)`.
   105	
   106	The draft’s E4 phrase “Tier 2 fails at 45°/R” conflates an intentionally unsupported transformation with failure of the claimed C4 invariance.
   107	
   108	**Concrete fix:** Register “Tier 2-C4” explicitly; exclude 45°/random from its pooled verdict; retain their dump distances as descriptive diagnostics.
   109	
   110	**Changes what Yixun must decide:** **Yes.** He must approve C4-only Tier 2 semantics for OrbitRIR.
