   112	## P4 — Attention backend and import shadow
   113	
   114	**Status: BLOCKING**
   115	
   116	The planner’s backend findings are confirmed:
   117	
   118	- `flash-attn` version `2.7.4.post1` is installed, with package, metadata and CUDA extension timestamps `2026-11-01 23:14:14 EST`.
   119	- FLAC imports it at [transformer.py:12](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/src/models/transformer.py:12).
   120	- The diffusion transformer selects it whenever importable, otherwise SDPA, at [transformer.py:406](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/src/models/transformer.py:406).
   121	- exp_25 logs and exp_22’s August logs print `No module named 'flash_attn'` and `flash_attn not installed`.
   122	
   123	A top-level `flash_attn` shadow that raises `ImportError` is functionally sufficient to force FLAC’s diffusion transformer onto SDPA without modifying the installed package. I found no other code in the `eval_FLAC.py` path that would change B-F behavior because of the shadow. The DINO conditioner is loaded through `AutoModel` without an explicit flash implementation at [conditioners.py:445](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/src/models/conditioners.py:445); its current default remains SDPA.
   124	
   125	But the proposed **scratch** shadow is not provenance-safe. The exp_25 runner hashes only its enumerated relevant tree at [depth_canon_eval_run.sh:111](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_eval_run.sh:111). An external scratch directory is absent from the campaign digest, so the evaluated backend input would be uncommitted and unhashed.
   126	
   127	Also, `eval_localization.py` records `flash_attn_available` using `find_spec`, not the actual transformer dispatch, at [eval_localization.py:719](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/eval_localization.py:719) and [eval_localization.py:863](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/eval_localization.py:863). A shadow package still has a discoverable spec, so exp_22 would misleadingly record “available” even though the FLAC import fell back.
   128	
   129	The two exact P1 controls are a proportionate launch gate if they compare the old/new waveform manifests and stream hashes bit-for-bit. Combined with the source diff—only `src/localization/*` changed since `d6ca307a`—they establish the intended P1 evaluator-path equivalence. They do not prove universal equivalence, and “inside the vanilla envelope” is not an acceptable fallback for E1.
